{
    desc => ':set cursorline highlights the current line',
    description => <<'END_DESC',
Macro: `xt/visual/macros/set_cursorline`

Tests that `:set cursorline` adds a background highlight to the current
cursor line, making it visually distinct.

Ex: `:set cursorline`

- **set_cursorline_initial.png**: No cursor line highlight; all lines have the same background.
- **set_cursorline_after_set.png**: Line 1 highlighted with cursorline background color; cursor sits on the highlighted line.
END_DESC
    run => sub {
        my ($ctx) = @_;
        $ctx->buffer->set_text($CODE);
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('initial');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->ex('set cursorline');
        $ctx->delay(200);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_set');
    },
}
